  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The query is a 4-anilinoquinazoline with the same 3-chloro-4-fluoroaniline and quinazoline core as gefitinib and afatinib; L4 records classify gefitinib as BCS class II with high Caco-2 permeability and human small-intestinal Peff of 1.2 × 10^-4 cm/s, and vandetanib, erlotinib, and HMPL-013 also show high permeability, supporting high intestinal permeability for this scaffold.",
      "card_ids": ["C46","C56","C50","C49","C55","C45"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 oral exposure records for erlotinib show substantial Cmax after oral dosing (geometric mean 1.83 µg/mL fasting and 2.64 µg/mL post-meal), consistent with meaningful oral absorption in the 4-anilinoquinazoline class.",
      "card_ids": ["C41","C37","C43"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 records show gefitinib is an ABCG2/ABCB1 substrate and afatinib exposure is modulated by P-gp inhibitors/inducers, indicating gut-wall efflux can affect absorption; however, neither record reports an absolute F value, so this is mechanistic and not affirmative evidence for F < 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C58","C67"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 bidirectional permeability records for compounds bearing 3-chloro-4-fluorophenyl and piperidine motifs show high A-B Papp with efflux ratios below 1, supportive of high permeability, though these are not the query scaffold and carry lower transferability.",
      "card_ids": ["C63","C61"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 hepatic-clearance records for the closest analog afatinib show low mouse liver microsomal CLint (9.4 µL/min/mg), while neratinib shows moderate-to-high HLM CLint (39-42 µL/min/mg) and high mouse CLint (126 µL/min/mg), and poziotinib shows moderate HLM CLint (22 µL/min/mg); these are in vitro, species-specific, and not direct oral-bioavailability outcomes, so they do not establish F < 20% for the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C77","C72","C69","C80","C75","C70"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "C73 reports BIBX1382, a quinazoline, was relatively stable in human liver microsomes yet had high in vivo clearance after IV dosing, but no oral F is reported and the structure is not the query; this raises uncertainty about translating microsomal stability to F but is not affirmative low evidence.",
      "card_ids": ["C73"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "C78 shows gefitinib is metabolized by CYP3A4, CYP3A5, CYP2D6, and CYP1A1, but the record reports no absolute F value; CYP metabolism alone is not affirmative evidence for F < 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C78"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Direct low-F L1 references (raloxifene ~2%, bazedoxifene ~6.2%, avanafil 8-10%) are structurally unrelated to the query, and their low F is attributed to phenolic glucuronidation or first-pass metabolism liabilities not present in the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C01","C09","C15"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C69","C70","C71","C72","C73","C74","C75","C76","C77","C78","C79","C80"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability (oral vs IV) measurement for the query.",
    "No query-specific hepatic clearance or metabolic stability assay; L6 records are for afatinib, neratinib, poziotinib, gefitinib, and other analogs, not the query itself.",
    "No query-specific human PK, dose, formulation, or food-effect data.",
    "L6 HLM/MLM CLint values are in vitro and species-specific; translation to human first-pass extraction and F is uncertain.",
    "The query's piperidine-acrylamide side chain and 7-methoxy group may alter metabolic stability relative to afatinib/gefitinib, but no direct data are available.",
    "No direct evidence of F < 20% for any structurally related molecule; BIBX1382 high in vivo clearance lacks an oral F value."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Prediction remains high: the query's 4-anilinoquinazoline scaffold is supported by high-permeability records for gefitinib, vandetanib, erlotinib, and HMPL-013, substantial oral Cmax for erlotinib, and low mouse microsomal CLint for afatinib, the closest analog. L6 hepatic-clearance records for neratinib/poziotinib show moderate-to-high HLM CLint but no direct F < 20% outcome and are not query-specific; they do not provide affirmative threshold-relevant evidence for low. Confidence remains moderate."
}

